However, the second transaction already did `compareAndSetStatus`? No — second sees status RELEASED (not RELEASABLE), so goes to else branch, no state change. Good.

One concern: DuplicateKeyException caught inside @Transactional — in Spring, catching it doesn't mark rollback-only (that's only for exceptions propagating through proxy). Fine.

Another subtlety: expired check uses `now.isAfter(expireAt)` — at exactly boundary, isAfter false → allowed. Correct per spec ("恰在效期边界时刻仍可放行").

