DTOs:
- CheckInRequest { @NotBlank barcode, @NotBlank componentType, @NotNull LocalDate expireDate }
- TestResultRequest { @NotNull TestType testType, @NotNull TestOutcome result }
- ReleaseRequestDto { @NotBlank requestId, @NotBlank barcode, @NotNull Instant windowStart, @NotNull Instant windowEnd }

Responses: use records directly (BloodUnit → UnitResponse to avoid exposing id? fine to expose). I'll map BloodUnit to UnitResponse {barcode, componentType, status, initialResult, recheckResult, expireAt}.

Controllers:
- BloodUnitController: POST /api/units, POST /api/units/{barcode}/test-results, GET /api/units/{barcode}
- ReleaseController: POST /api/releases

Exception handler: @RestControllerAdvice handling ApiException → status + {error: message}; validation errors → 400.

Note application.yaml sets server.error.include-message: never — that's for the default error controller; our @RestControllerAdvice returns our own body, fine.

